  "id": "Compound::DB01438 - Gene::6332",
  "verbalization": "Phenazopyridine appears to interact with voltage-gated sodium channels through a shared mechanism involving Scn7a, as evidenced by its binding to multiple subunits of the same class of channels—Scn11a, Scn8a, and Scn2a. These subunits participate in voltage-gated sodium channel activity, which is ultimately participated by Scn7a. The high scores in the paths suggest a consistent and significant interaction between Phenazopyridine and the sodium channel activity pathway, with Scn7a being a key component of this process. The overlapping roles of the subunits indicate that Phenazopyridine may modulate sodium channel function through a common pathway, potentially influencing the activity of Scn7a. The evidence supports a relationship where Phenazopyridine interacts with sodium channels, which in turn are involved in the activity of Scn7a, suggesting a possible role in neuronal signaling or other physiological processes.",
